1
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Three magical wishes. One life changing adventure.

2
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Wish Dragon is a animation, family, comedy film directed by Chris Appelhans.

3
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Determined teen Din is longing to reconnect with his childhood best friend when he
meets a wish-granting dragon who shows him the magic of possibilities.

4
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Din (voice), played by Jimmy Wong.

5
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Long (voice), played by John Cho.

6
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Mom (voice), played by Constance Wu.

7
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
Lina (voice), played by Natasha Liu Bordizzo.

8
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Short Goon / Security Guard 2 (voice), played by Jimmy O. Yang.

9
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Pockets (voice), played by Aaron Yoo.

10
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Wish Dragon is a 2021 animated fantasy comedy film written and directed
by Chris Appelhans in his feature film directorial debut.

11
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
The film stars Jimmy Wong, John Cho, Constance
Wu, Natasha Liu Bordizzo, Jimmy O.

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Yang, Aaron Yoo, Will Yun Lee, and Ronny Chieng.

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
Jackie Chan produced the film and voiced Cho's role
in the Chinese Mandarin version.

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
It tells the story about a college student named Din Song, who encounters a teapot
inhabited by a dragon named Long, who has the power to grant three wishes.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
Wish Dragon was released theatrically in China on January 15, 2021,
and on Netflix internationally on June 11, 2021.

16
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
A sequel is set to be released in Summer 2027
with Appelhans returning as writer.

17
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
